+# Free-Text Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so its provenance stayed open.
+
+The owner has now asked for the veterinarian directory to be narrowed to one specialty (2026-09-17). That request meets NG-9 head on: read widely, the row forbids it; read narrowly, the row forbids only search. The owner decided the narrow reading.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 whole.** Refuse the request as declined scope. Rejected: the owner owns the boundary and has decided otherwise.
+2. **Drop NG-9.** Open veterinarian search along with the narrowing. Rejected: it concedes the larger capability nobody asked for, and the row's rationale still holds for free-text search.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Free-text search over veterinarians, pets, and visits stays out of scope. Narrowing the veterinarian directory to an attribute it already displays is in scope, and specialty is the first such attribute.
+
+The distinction is the boundary: a search takes text the reader composes and matches it loosely. A narrowing takes one value the directory already shows and matches it whole. The directory gains no free-text field, no partial matching, and no search results page.
+
+A later request for veterinarian search proceeds only on an explicit owner decision recorded at intake, exactly as before. This narrowing settles NG-9's provenance for that row alone.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation; the Non-Goals preamble names it decided. Every row other than NG-4, NG-5, and NG-9 remains part of it.
+- Narrowing the directory by another attribute it already shows is now a scoping question rather than a boundary reversal.
+- Pet and visit search remain wholly declined; nothing here weakens them.
+- Prefix matching stays a property of owner search alone. The specialty narrowing matches the whole name, so the two do not converge by accident.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
