+# Specialty-Narrowed Veterinarian Reads Are Not Cached
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+Every read on `VetRepository` today is annotated `@Cacheable("vets")`. `CacheConfiguration` creates that cache from a JCache `MutableConfiguration` with statistics enabled. It sets no size limit and no eviction policy; the source comment records that a size limit needs the JCache provider's own mechanism, which this project does not configure.
+
+`REQ-VET-003` adds a read narrowed by a specialty name taken from the request. Extending the existing annotation to it would make free-form caller text a cache key.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Cache the narrowed read in the `vets` cache.** Consistent with the two existing reads and free to write. Rejected: an unevicted cache keyed by caller-supplied text grows without bound in both entry count and key size, which a reader of a demonstration application would copy.
+2. **Cache it in a second, bounded cache.** Rejected: bounding needs provider-specific configuration the project does not have, and a dedicated cache for one query is more machinery than the capability justifies.
+3. **Leave the narrowed read uncached** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+The specialty-narrowed read queries the database on every request. The two unnarrowed reads keep their caching unchanged.
+
+This departs from the local convention that every `VetRepository` read is cached. The departure's reason is the cache's unbounded configuration, not a judgment about caching.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A narrowed directory request costs one query. The seeded directory holds six veterinarians, so the query is small.
+- No caller can grow the heap by varying the specialty name. The paged unnarrowed read stays keyed by the requested page number, which is unchanged by this decision.
+- The two vet read paths now differ in their caching. A reader of `VetRepository` sees one annotated method and one that is not, and this record is the explanation.
+- Giving the `vets` cache a size limit and an eviction policy would reduce this to a plain consistency question. That configuration is the trigger for revisiting this record, and it is tracked as the open question on vet cache invalidation.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vet/VetRepository.java` — the narrowed read.
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/system/CacheConfiguration.java` — the cache this read stays out of.
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the veterinarian directory's two surfaces and its narrowing contract.
+- [system-design.md § Threat Model](../system-design.md#threat-model) — the cache-growth row this decision closes.
+- [system-design.md § Open Questions from the Survey](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey) — vet cache invalidation.
